  <static seed="124" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec7/Q07.pg">
    <statement><p>Find <m>dy/dx</m> in terms of <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> 
if <m>x^{4} y - x - 2 y - 7 =0</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{dy}{dx} =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1-4x^{3}y}{x^{4}-2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>We differentiate implicitly with respect to <m>x</m>.  
This gives
<me>4 x^{3} y - x^{4} \, \frac{dy}{dx}
- 1 - 2 \, \frac{dy}{dx} = 0,</me>
or
<me>(x^{4}-2) \, \frac{dy}{dx} = 1-4x^{3}y,</me>
and so
<me>\frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{1 - 4 x^{3} y}{x^{4} - 2}.</me></p>
</solution>
